<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammadjan Tynyshbaev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mukhamedzhan Tynyshpaev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammadjan Tynyshbaev was a Kazakh engineer and politician of the Alash movement who served as the first head of government of the Turkestan Autonomy, proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> in November 1917. He soon handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-chokay">Mustafa Chokay</a>, and the Bolsheviks crushed the autonomy in February 1918. Later a railway engineer and historian, he was shot during Stalin's purges in 1937.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammadjan-tynyshbaev.jpg" alt="Muhammadjan Tynyshbaev" width="256" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tynyshpayev_M.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
